+### §stable-tab-keys — closing a tab renumbers the others so keys stay contiguous
+- Since: 2026-10-23, when the maintainer explicitly overrode the original 2026-09-02 decision (see Superseded).
+- Decision: `closeTab` renumbers the remaining tabs, in their existing order, to `t1…tn` and sets `next` to n+1. Keys
+  never have gaps (closing `t2` of `t1,t2,t3` gives `t1,t2`), and the next tab opened continues the sequence (`t3`).
+- Forbidden: leaving a gap in the keys after a close.
+- Reason: the maintainer's decision on 2026-10-23; no further rationale recorded. Known trade-off: the key is the React
+  key and the URL state, so every tab to the right of the closed one gets a new key and remounts.
+- Superseded (2026-09-02 → 2026-10-23): a key was assigned once from `next` and never reused or shifted; closing a tab
+  left a gap (`t1,t3`) and renumbering was forbidden, because shifting keys remounted the tabs to the right and dropped
+  their scroll position and unsaved form input (incident 2026-08-29, reproduced by the former "close keeps keys" test).
+  The anchor keeps its original name so existing references still resolve.
 - Evidence: `tab-keys.test.mjs`
